1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,990
One crore rupees.

2
00:00:02,030 --> 00:00:04,230
It's the number everyone in India talks

3
00:00:04,270 --> 00:00:04,760
about.

4
00:00:04,830 --> 00:00:07,270
The salary goal, the retirement goal,

5
00:00:07,310 --> 00:00:09,670
the number that means you've made it.

6
00:00:09,710 --> 00:00:12,630
But almost nobody has actually seen it.

7
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:13,800
So let's build it.

8
00:00:13,950 --> 00:00:15,880
Right here, to scale.

9
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:18,665
And once we've built it,

10
00:00:18,705 --> 00:00:20,665
we'll ask three questions.

11
00:00:20,705 --> 00:00:23,105
How long does it really take to get there?

12
00:00:23,145 --> 00:00:25,315
What will it actually be worth when you

13
00:00:25,385 --> 00:00:25,745
do?

14
00:00:25,785 --> 00:00:28,035
And is it even enough?

15
00:00:31,433 --> 00:00:33,233
Start with one note.

16
00:00:33,273 --> 00:00:35,353
A five hundred rupee note is a hundred and

17
00:00:35,393 --> 00:00:37,713
fifty millimetres long and sixty-six

18
00:00:37,753 --> 00:00:39,193
millimetres wide.

19
00:00:39,233 --> 00:00:41,393
Reserve Bank specifications put its

20
00:00:41,433 --> 00:00:43,153
thickness at around a hundred and ten

21
00:00:43,193 --> 00:00:44,193
microns.

22
00:00:44,233 --> 00:00:46,403
About a tenth of a millimetre.

23
00:00:47,183 --> 00:00:48,983
Put a hundred of them together,

24
00:00:49,023 --> 00:00:50,543
and you get a bundle.

25
00:00:50,583 --> 00:00:53,223
Fifty thousand rupees, about eleven

26
00:00:53,263 --> 00:00:54,663
millimetres tall.

27
00:00:54,703 --> 00:00:56,873
A little over a centimetre.

28
00:00:57,600 --> 00:00:58,920
Now keep going.

29
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:01,000
One crore rupees in five hundred rupee

30
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:03,560
notes is twenty thousand notes.

31
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:05,720
That's two hundred bundles.

32
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:07,160
Stacked on top of each other,

33
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,293
they reach two point two metres.

34
00:01:09,333 --> 00:01:11,160
Taller than the average person standing

35
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:12,410
next to it.

36
00:01:14,683 --> 00:01:17,003
And that's the compact version.

37
00:01:17,043 --> 00:01:18,643
Switch to hundred rupee notes,

38
00:01:18,683 --> 00:01:21,523
and one crore becomes one lakh notes.

39
00:01:21,563 --> 00:01:24,003
Stacked up, that's eleven metres,

40
00:01:24,043 --> 00:01:25,733
about the height of a three storey

41
00:01:25,963 --> 00:01:26,483
building.

42
00:01:26,523 --> 00:01:29,603
In ten rupee notes, it's ten lakh notes.

43
00:01:29,643 --> 00:01:31,803
A hundred and ten metres tall.

44
00:01:31,843 --> 00:01:33,403
One and a half times the height of the

45
00:01:33,443 --> 00:01:34,853
Qutub Minar.

46
00:01:37,517 --> 00:01:39,557
If you counted every note,

47
00:01:39,597 --> 00:01:42,517
one per second, without a single break,

48
00:01:42,557 --> 00:01:44,597
you'd be counting for five and a half

49
00:01:44,637 --> 00:01:45,504
hours.

50
00:01:45,544 --> 00:01:47,317
And that's just counting it.

51
00:01:47,357 --> 00:01:50,167
Earning it is a very different story.

52
00:01:54,017 --> 00:01:56,057
Let's say you can put aside twenty

53
00:01:56,097 --> 00:01:58,137
thousand rupees every month.

54
00:01:58,177 --> 00:02:00,297
That's a serious amount of discipline for

55
00:02:00,337 --> 00:02:01,657
most households.

56
00:02:01,697 --> 00:02:04,137
Every month, one more stack of notes goes

57
00:02:04,177 --> 00:02:05,627
onto the tower.

58
00:02:06,308 --> 00:02:08,108
If that money just sits there,

59
00:02:08,148 --> 00:02:10,748
earning nothing, the tower grows in a

60
00:02:10,788 --> 00:02:12,268
perfectly straight line.

61
00:02:12,308 --> 00:02:14,988
Two lakh forty thousand rupees a year.

62
00:02:15,028 --> 00:02:17,188
To reach one crore, you'd need five

63
00:02:17,228 --> 00:02:18,375
hundred months.

64
00:02:18,415 --> 00:02:21,068
That's forty-one years and eight months.

65
00:02:21,108 --> 00:02:23,428
Start at twenty-five, and you finish at

66
00:02:23,468 --> 00:02:24,958
sixty-six.

67
00:02:29,392 --> 00:02:31,512
Now let's build a second tower.

68
00:02:31,552 --> 00:02:33,192
Same twenty thousand rupees,

69
00:02:33,232 --> 00:02:34,232
every month.

70
00:02:34,272 --> 00:02:36,792
But this time, the money is invested,

71
00:02:36,832 --> 00:02:37,992
and it grows.

72
00:02:38,032 --> 00:02:40,072
For this example, we'll assume twelve

73
00:02:40,112 --> 00:02:41,352
percent a year.

74
00:02:41,392 --> 00:02:43,592
That's an assumption, not a promise.

75
00:02:43,632 --> 00:02:45,859
Real returns go up and down,

76
00:02:45,899 --> 00:02:47,482
and they can be lower.

77
00:02:48,183 --> 00:02:49,663
For the first few years,

78
00:02:49,703 --> 00:02:52,703
the two towers look almost identical.

79
00:02:52,743 --> 00:02:55,263
After one year, the invested tower is

80
00:02:55,303 --> 00:02:58,063
ahead by just sixteen thousand rupees.

81
00:02:58,103 --> 00:02:59,663
It barely shows.

82
00:02:59,703 --> 00:03:01,583
This is the part where most people give

83
00:03:01,623 --> 00:03:02,513
up.

84
00:03:03,225 --> 00:03:05,545
But growth earns growth.

85
00:03:05,585 --> 00:03:08,505
By year ten, the invested tower adds more

86
00:03:08,545 --> 00:03:11,105
than five lakh rupees in a single year,

87
00:03:11,145 --> 00:03:13,025
just from its own returns.

88
00:03:13,065 --> 00:03:15,932
By year fourteen, almost ten lakh.

89
00:03:15,972 --> 00:03:17,692
The line stops being straight,

90
00:03:17,732 --> 00:03:20,035
and starts to bend upwards.

91
00:03:20,725 --> 00:03:23,325
The invested tower reaches one crore in

92
00:03:23,365 --> 00:03:25,085
about fifteen years.

93
00:03:25,125 --> 00:03:27,805
At that moment, the savings tower is only

94
00:03:27,845 --> 00:03:29,885
about a third of the way up.

95
00:03:29,925 --> 00:03:32,445
Same money from your pocket every month.

96
00:03:32,485 --> 00:03:35,135
Almost twenty-seven years sooner.

97
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:40,120
And here's the part that surprises people.

98
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:42,880
Of that one crore, you only put in about

99
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:44,387
thirty-six lakh.

100
00:03:44,427 --> 00:03:47,000
The other sixty-four lakh is growth.

101
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:49,560
Most of the tower isn't your money at all.

102
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:51,130
It's time.

103
00:03:52,975 --> 00:03:55,335
Change the assumption, and the finish line

104
00:03:55,375 --> 00:03:56,375
moves.

105
00:03:56,415 --> 00:03:58,615
At ten percent a year, it takes a little

106
00:03:58,655 --> 00:04:00,775
under sixteen and a half years.

107
00:04:00,815 --> 00:04:03,575
At eight percent, a little over eighteen.

108
00:04:03,615 --> 00:04:06,295
Slower, but every one of them still beats

109
00:04:06,335 --> 00:04:09,225
saving alone by more than two decades.

110
00:04:12,517 --> 00:04:13,917
But there's a catch.

111
00:04:13,957 --> 00:04:16,677
A crore in twenty years won't be the same

112
00:04:16,717 --> 00:04:18,370
crore as today.

113
00:04:18,410 --> 00:04:19,517
Prices rise.

114
00:04:19,557 --> 00:04:21,797
The Reserve Bank's inflation target is

115
00:04:21,837 --> 00:04:23,197
four percent a year.

116
00:04:23,237 --> 00:04:25,677
At four percent, a crore twenty years from

117
00:04:25,717 --> 00:04:28,557
now buys what about forty-six lakh buys

118
00:04:28,597 --> 00:04:29,357
today.

119
00:04:29,397 --> 00:04:31,837
At six percent, it's closer to thirty-one

120
00:04:31,877 --> 00:04:32,847
lakh.

121
00:04:34,517 --> 00:04:36,637
The tower stays the same height.

122
00:04:36,677 --> 00:04:39,117
The number printed on it stays the same.

123
00:04:39,157 --> 00:04:41,677
But what it can actually buy quietly

124
00:04:41,717 --> 00:04:44,607
shrinks, every single year.

125
00:04:48,642 --> 00:04:52,042
So, is one crore enough to retire on?

126
00:04:52,082 --> 00:04:54,482
One common rule of thumb says you can take

127
00:04:54,522 --> 00:04:56,522
out about four percent a year.

128
00:04:56,562 --> 00:04:59,082
On one crore, that's four lakh rupees a

129
00:04:59,122 --> 00:05:01,402
year, or roughly thirty-three thousand a

130
00:05:01,442 --> 00:05:02,412
month.

131
00:05:03,142 --> 00:05:05,662
That rule comes from American research,

132
00:05:05,702 --> 00:05:07,902
and India's higher inflation makes it

133
00:05:07,942 --> 00:05:09,182
optimistic here.

134
00:05:09,222 --> 00:05:11,742
And if you retire twenty years from now,

135
00:05:11,782 --> 00:05:13,582
with six percent inflation,

136
00:05:13,622 --> 00:05:15,422
that thirty-three thousand a month would

137
00:05:15,462 --> 00:05:17,982
feel like about ten thousand does today.

138
00:05:18,022 --> 00:05:21,075
For most families, that isn't retirement.

139
00:05:21,115 --> 00:05:22,592
It's a start.

140
00:05:26,642 --> 00:05:29,162
So what actually changes the picture?

141
00:05:29,202 --> 00:05:30,362
Two levers.

142
00:05:30,402 --> 00:05:32,842
The first is raising your investment every

143
00:05:32,882 --> 00:05:34,682
year, as your income grows.

144
00:05:34,722 --> 00:05:36,415
Start at twenty thousand a month,

145
00:05:36,455 --> 00:05:39,082
and increase it by ten percent every year.

146
00:05:39,122 --> 00:05:41,162
At the same assumed twelve percent,

147
00:05:41,202 --> 00:05:43,562
you reach one crore in about twelve years

148
00:05:43,602 --> 00:05:44,762
instead of fifteen.

149
00:05:44,802 --> 00:05:47,002
Even a five percent yearly increase gets

150
00:05:47,042 --> 00:05:49,452
you there in about thirteen and a half.

151
00:05:50,142 --> 00:05:52,182
The second lever is time,

152
00:05:52,222 --> 00:05:54,662
and it's the one you can never buy back.

153
00:05:54,702 --> 00:05:56,502
Take ten thousand rupees a month,

154
00:05:56,542 --> 00:05:58,422
invested until you're sixty,

155
00:05:58,462 --> 00:06:00,822
at the same assumed twelve percent.

156
00:06:00,862 --> 00:06:02,742
Start at twenty-five, and the tower

157
00:06:02,782 --> 00:06:05,142
reaches about six and a half crore.

158
00:06:05,182 --> 00:06:07,302
Start at thirty, about three and a half

159
00:06:07,342 --> 00:06:08,102
crore.

160
00:06:08,142 --> 00:06:10,582
Start at thirty-five, a little under two

161
00:06:10,622 --> 00:06:11,592
crore.

162
00:06:13,517 --> 00:06:16,277
Every five years you wait roughly halves

163
00:06:16,317 --> 00:06:18,597
the final tower, even though you only

164
00:06:18,637 --> 00:06:21,157
invest about six lakh rupees less.

165
00:06:21,197 --> 00:06:22,970
Or look at it the other way.

166
00:06:23,010 --> 00:06:25,210
To reach one crore in twenty years,

167
00:06:25,250 --> 00:06:27,397
you'd need about ten thousand a month.

168
00:06:27,437 --> 00:06:30,037
In fifteen years, about twenty thousand.

169
00:06:30,077 --> 00:06:32,624
In ten years, forty-three thousand.

170
00:06:32,664 --> 00:06:34,517
The later you start, the bigger the

171
00:06:34,557 --> 00:06:35,927
monthly bill.

172
00:06:37,392 --> 00:06:40,072
So here's what one crore really is.

173
00:06:40,112 --> 00:06:42,472
A stack of notes, two point two metres

174
00:06:42,512 --> 00:06:43,272
tall.

175
00:06:43,312 --> 00:06:45,912
Forty-one years if you only save.

176
00:06:45,952 --> 00:06:48,392
About fifteen if you invest and stay

177
00:06:48,432 --> 00:06:49,272
patient.

178
00:06:49,312 --> 00:06:51,352
And, by the time you get there,

179
00:06:51,392 --> 00:06:53,432
worth a lot less than it looks.

180
00:06:53,472 --> 00:06:55,112
The number stays the same.

181
00:06:55,152 --> 00:06:57,002
The size doesn't.

182
00:06:59,475 --> 00:07:01,435
This video is education,

183
00:07:01,475 --> 00:07:03,142
not financial advice.

184
00:07:03,182 --> 00:07:05,595
If you want to see money at its real size,

185
00:07:05,635 --> 00:07:06,675
subscribe.

186
00:07:06,715 --> 00:07:08,795
Next time, we're stacking up what a home

187
00:07:08,835 --> 00:07:10,605
loan really costs you.

